 "text": "The Paps of Anu are a mythological site in Ireland. They are two breast-shaped mountains in County Munster, the southwest province. The site is also called the Paps of Danu and Dá Chich Anann. The Paps lie near the Lakes of Killarney on the road from Cork. The two hills are nearly identical in size and shape. Cairns and stone structures crown their summits. Local tradition calls the mountains the Paps of Danu.",
